      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nOrder resident HiSparse block-table creation before sparse-index conversion, fixing invalid KV indices and FlashMLA startup crashes.\n\n## Claims\n\nOne device-stream dependency on the first index-group layer; no host synchronization.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/v1/attention/test_sparse_mla_backends.py -q -k 'hisparse or index_group or sparse_mqa'\n```\n\nH100: **47 passed**; both extended regression cases fail without the fix. Pre-commit passes.\n\nGLM-5.3, 8 H100s, TP8/EP8, MTP3, CUDA graphs, 64 GiB HiSparse, 32 GiB CPU weight offload/rank: **26 HTTP-200 requests**, including 6,331-token context, 128-token decode, 6,208-token prefix reuse and nonzero MTP acceptance. GSM8K smoke: **19/20** (first 20 questions, zero-shot, concurrency 4; no unpatched accuracy baseline).\n\n## Details\n\n`batch_block_table()` queues its producer after `logical_topk_ready`, previously the side converter’s only dependency. Follow-up to #60647 and #60417. Extends the existing stride test. Open-PR searches found no duplicate fix.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull Request Checklist</summary>\n\n- [x] Used the PR checklist.\n- [x] Design fit: dependency stays in the HiSparse resident path.\n- [x] Testing: failing regression and passing H100 checks.\n- [x] Code quality: pre-commit passes.\n- [x] Contents: root cause, validation and limits documented.\n</details>\n",
